---
/**
 * Tokens lesson — illustration #2 of 3.
 *
 * The vocab-vs-sequence tradeoff, rendered as a 1D spectrum: char-only
 * on the left (small vocab, huge sequences), word-only on the right
 * (giant vocab, OOV failures), subword in the middle as the engineering
 * compromise.
 *
 * Why a spectrum, not a comparison table:
 *   The lesson's pedagogical point is that subword is in between two
 *   pathological extremes. A spectrum shows that geometrically; a
 *   table makes the three options look co-equal.
 */
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 800 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="tradeoff-title tradeoff-desc">
		<title id="tradeoff-title">The vocabulary-versus-sequence-length tradeoff</title>
		<desc id="tradeoff-desc">A horizontal spectrum. On the left, "one token per character": small vocabulary of about 200 entries, but sequences become 5 to 10 times longer. Marked with a red cross. On the right, "one token per word": vocabulary of millions of entries, plus out-of-vocabulary failures. Also marked with a red cross. In the middle, "subword (BPE)": vocabulary of 30,000 to 100,000 entries, moderate sequence length, marked with a green check, labeled "the engineering compromise."</desc>
		<line x1="60" y1="60" x2="740" y2="60" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.4"/>
		<text x="60" y="40" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">small vocab, long sequences</text>
		<text x="740" y="40" text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">huge vocab, OOV failures</text>
		<circle cx="100" cy="60" r="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="100" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">one per character</text>
		<text x="100" y="115" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">about 200 entries</text>
		<text x="100" y="133" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">5 to 10 times longer</text>
		<text x="100" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="22" fill="#dc2626" font-weight="600">✗</text>
		<circle cx="700" cy="60" r="8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
		<text x="700" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">one per word</text>
		<text x="700" y="115" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">millions of entries</text>
		<text x="700" y="133" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">vocabulary blowup, OOV</text>
		<text x="700" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="22" fill="#dc2626" font-weight="600">✗</text>
		<circle cx="400" cy="60" r="13" fill="#7c3aed"/>
		<text x="400" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">subword (BPE)</text>
		<text x="400" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">30k to 100k entries</text>
		<text x="400" y="138" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">moderate sequence length</text>
		<text x="400" y="175" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="24" fill="#16a34a" font-weight="700">✓</text>
		<text x="400" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#7c3aed" font-style="italic">the engineering compromise</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>Why subword tokenization wins. Both extremes break in different ways; the middle is the only place that works at scale.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus {
		margin: 1.75rem auto;
		max-width: 100%;
	}
	.cw-illus svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 780px;
		height: auto;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.cw-illus figcaption {
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		opacity: 0.75;
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
